{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the input-to-output residual skip with a conv loses the residual path, so the gain is smaller than when replacing none/pool/1x1."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a weak pooling shortcut costs little compared with removing a skip or conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 already absent, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 3 feeding the output, collapsing the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct shortcut, edge 5 carries more of the output so cutting it hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 does not connect directly to the output, deleting its input matters less."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "If node 2 has no outgoing edge, edge 1 is dead so removing it has near-zero effect instead of a loss."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling with identity is beneficial, whereas replacing a conv3x3 with identity loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a learned conv for pooling costs more than swapping none or skip for pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Losing a conv3x3 on the node1-to-output edge hurts more than replacing skip, none or 1x1 with poolin